# The shelf is set up in a step of its own that decides nothing: the folder is the module's constant, `OUT`, which
# each method reads itself to name its file and hand the path to `write`. The file is whole in the method, on the calls
# that lead to `write`: under `keep_report` the route writes the report alone, under `keep_log` the log alone, as on the
# clean side. The shelf goes from the step that built it to `main` and to each method it runs on, whose body uses none
# of it.

route shelf.cli.main
step main/open_shelf
step main/open_shelf/Shelf()
step main/Shelf.keep_report
step main/Shelf.keep_report/write
step main/Shelf.keep_log
step main/Shelf.keep_log/write

line entry > main call
line main/open_shelf/Shelf() > Shelf@main/open_shelf/Shelf() value
line Shelf@main/open_shelf/Shelf() > main/open_shelf value               # the shelf built goes back
line main/open_shelf > Shelf·shelf@main/open_shelf value
line Shelf·shelf@main/open_shelf > main/Shelf.keep_report value           # the shelf the method runs on
line Shelf·shelf@main/open_shelf > main/Shelf.keep_log value
line main/Shelf.keep_report/write > File(out/report.txt) own
line main/Shelf.keep_log/write > File(out/log.txt) own

home Shelf@main/open_shelf/Shelf() main/open_shelf
home Shelf·shelf@main/open_shelf main

side entry left
side File(out/report.txt) right
side File(out/log.txt) right
